<title>SPAIN: El Aguila says Heineken talk unfounded.</title>
<headline>El Aguila says Heineken talk unfounded.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>An executive at Spanish brewer El Aguila on Thursday described as &quot;unfounded&quot; market talk that Dutch brewer Heineken wanted to raise its 65 percent stake to full 100 percent ownership.</p>
<p>&quot;These are rumours that resurface every six months. They have no foundation,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>Shares in El Aguila rose 12 pesetas to 692 in Madrid with around 214,000 shares traded - about 10 times its average daily volume.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom + 34 1 585-2159</p>
